Package: credentialsd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends:
 publicsuffix,
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 credentialsd-ui,
 dbus-user-session,
Suggests:
 credentialsd-webextension,
Description: credential manager service with WebAuthn/passkey support
 credentialsd is a D-Bus service that lets applications create and use
 WebAuthn credentials (passkeys) with security keys over USB, NFC and
 hybrid (caBLE) transports.
 .
 This package contains the daemon, its D-Bus activation file and systemd
 user unit.
 .
 Applications reach the service through the experimental Credential
 interface of xdg-desktop-portal, which is not in upstream
 xdg-desktop-portal yet and needs a patched build of it.

Package: credentialsd-ui
Architecture: linux-any
Depends:
 credentialsd (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Suggests:
 xdg-desktop-portal,
Description: credential manager service with WebAuthn/passkey support - GTK UI
 credentialsd is a D-Bus service that lets applications create and use
 WebAuthn credentials (passkeys) with security keys over USB, NFC and
 hybrid (caBLE) transports.
 .
 This package contains the GTK 4 dialog that asks the user to choose a
 device, enter a PIN or confirm a request, and the xdg-desktop-portal
 backend description that points the Credential portal at it.

Package: credentialsd-webextension
Architecture: all
Depends:
 credentialsd (>= ${source:Version}),
 python3,
 python3-dbus-next,
 ${misc:Depends},
Enhances:
 firefox,
 firefox-esr,
Description: credential manager service with WebAuthn/passkey support - browser helper
 credentialsd is a D-Bus service that lets applications create and use
 WebAuthn credentials (passkeys) with security keys over USB, NFC and
 hybrid (caBLE) transports.
 .
 This package contains the native messaging host that connects the
 credentialsd browser extension to the service, for Firefox builds without
 native portal integration, and the unsigned extension archives for
 Firefox and Chromium. The native messaging host is registered for
 Firefox from the Debian package; Firefox installed as a Snap or Flatpak
 does not read it.
 .
 Release builds of Firefox only install signed extensions; upstream
 publishes a signed build of the extension with each release.
